  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules set 24-hour incident reporting and 72-hour customer notice, and keep the 55 °C test with a 5% limit, but they remove any sales stop and allow up to 24 months before restrictions with no interim cap, which mainly benefits Northwind's Hearth 10. The S5 recall trigger stays at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, so Halcyon's Ember 8 must be recalled, though the text explicitly states a recall is not a permanent market ban. Remote shut-off for installed units is set at 72 months and suppression at 36 months, both within the acceptable ranges."
